  'startup-budget': 'It works by itself at every start. Vex records three marks (scripts ready, window ready, everything settled) for the last ten starts on this computer. Features that are not needed at first paint appear a moment after the window opens.',
  'plan-preview': 'It shows by itself whenever an action would touch many things at once, such as the evening tab tidy-up, a downloads clean-out or closing many tabs. You see a dialog saying how many things it will do, each with a tick box, and a button to go ahead.',
  'provenance-chip': 'It shows by itself next to summaries, rewrites, search answers and drafted lines. You see a short label such as Vex AI, Local AI or Rule, and hovering it names the data the output was built from.',
  'first-use-sheet': 'The first time you use a feature marked new or beta, a small card appears over the window. It lists what the feature does, what it reads, writes and sends, and how to turn it off. You see it once per feature.',
  'download-guard': 'When a download looks like a cheat tool or a fake update, Vex saves it to a holding folder and shows a prompt with the reasons. The file stays there until you decide to keep or discard it.',
  'scroll-memory': 'It works by itself. Every few seconds and when you leave a tab, Vex notes where it is scrolled to and saves that with the tab in your session. After Ctrl+Shift+T or a restart, the page loads and then scrolls back to that spot.',
  'spell-lang': 'Right-click inside a text box or any editable field. You will see a Spelling language entry with the four choices, and on an underlined word an Add to dictionary entry. The choice is kept on this device.',
  'autoscroll': 'Press the middle button on an empty part of a page. A small mark appears where you pressed and the page follows the pointer. It listens only for the middle button and reads nothing from the page.',
  'load-failure': 'When a page cannot be reached, a Vex notice covers the tab with a short explanation of what happened and what to try, plus the buttons. The Wayback Machine and saved copy buttons appear only when they apply.',
  'gesture-editor': 'Open Settings and find Mouse gestures. Each stroke is listed with the action it runs, and you pick a different action from the list. Your choices are then used when you draw that stroke on a page.',
  'tab-select': 'Ctrl-click a tab to pick it. Picked tabs get an outline and a tint, and once two or more are picked a small bar floats under the tab strip with the buttons for them.',
  'tab-hold': 'Close a tab with its X and keep the pointer over the tab bar. The tabs after it slide left by one tab\'s width, so the next X lands where the last one was. Moving off the bar lets the strip fill out again.',
  'tab-thumbs': 'It works by itself. When you leave a tab, Vex keeps a small picture of it. If you return to that tab after it fell asleep, you see that picture instead of white while the page loads, for a few seconds at most.',
  'preconnect': 'It works by itself. When the pointer rests on a link for a moment, Vex quietly opens a connection to that link\'s site. You see nothing; the page just appears sooner when you click.',
  'mini-window': 'When another program opens a link in Vex, a small window shows that page instead of adding a tab. Without it, the link opens as it normally would.',
  'jump-list': 'Right-click the Vex icon on the Windows taskbar. The jump list shows the four actions, and choosing one runs it in Vex.',
  'panel-guard': 'Nothing to press. When Game mode sees a game start and a hidden panel keeps using a lot of processor for about a minute, Vex sleeps it. When the game ends you get one message saying so, and Why did that happen? has an Undo that opens the panel again.',
  'net-courtesy': 'Nothing to press. When Game mode sees a game start, downloads in progress are paused, and so is any download that starts during the game. After the game they resume, and you see a count such as Vex used 14 MB, with an Undo in Why did that happen?.',
  'job-tools-offer': 'Nothing to press. Once a day Vex checks which Toolbox tools you used; if several are missing from your list, a suggestion appears in the Attention Inbox titled Your Toolbox list could follow what you use, with a Use my most used button.',
  'brief-cards': 'Nothing to press. A card appears on the New Tab or in the Morning Brief only when there is something to show, such as 3 sites can use your mic, a service reporting a major incident, a highlight due to come back, or a flagged page that changed. The service status card stays off until you switch it on.',
